---
globs: frontend/src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

[LANG][!JAVASCRIPT] This is a React project. All tests use Vitest with React Testing Library.

[TEST][!FOCUSED] Write focused unit tests that are isolated and follow React testing best practices.

[RUN][!COMMAND] Run frontend tests with: `cd frontend && npm run test -- --run`

[WATCH][!DEV] During development, use watch mode: `cd frontend && npm test`

[TOOLS][!TESTING-LIBRARY] Use React Testing Library for component testing:
  - Use `render()` to mount components
  - Query by role/label/text (not implementation details)
  - Use `fireEvent` or `userEvent` for interactions
  - Use `waitFor` for async assertions
  
[SPEED][!PROFILE] EVERY test MUST declare speed_profile before the test:
  ```javascript
  const speed_profile = (profile) => (name, fn) => {
    const timeouts = { fast: 1000, medium: 5000, slow: 30000 };
    return test(name, fn, timeouts[profile]);
  };
  
  speed_profile("fast")("renders correctly", () => {
    // Test implementation
  });
  
  speed_profile("medium")("calls real API", async () => {
    // Test with API call
  });
  ```

[SPEED][!CATEGORIES] Speed profile guidelines:
  - fast (< 1s): Pure rendering, state updates, validation
  - medium (< 5s): Real API calls, file I/O
  - slow (< 30s): Integration tests, LLM calls

[NO-MOCK][!REAL] Never mock. Use real implementations:
  - Real stores with real state
  - Real API calls (or skip if unavailable)
  - Real data from factories
  - If external system unavailable, skip explicitly

[ASSERTIONS][!ACCESSIBLE] Prefer accessible queries:
  - `getByRole()` - BEST for interactive elements
  - `getByLabelText()` - BEST for form inputs
  - `getByText()` - OK for static content
  - Avoid `getByTestId()` unless necessary

[SETUP][!ISOLATION] Each test should be isolated:
  - Clear all mocks in `beforeEach`
  - Don't rely on test execution order
  - Reset component state between tests

[COVERAGE][!COMPREHENSIVE] Test the following for each component:
  - Rendering with default props
  - User interactions (clicks, typing, form submission)
  - Conditional rendering (loading, error, success states)
  - Props validation and edge cases
  - State updates and side effects

[STRUCTURE][!ORGANIZED] Organize tests logically:
  ```javascript
  describe("ComponentName", () => {
    const defaultProps = { /* ... */ };
    
    beforeEach(() => {
      vi.clearAllMocks();
    });
    
    test("renders with required props", () => { /* ... */ });
    test("handles user interaction", () => { /* ... */ });
    test("displays error state", () => { /* ... */ });
  });
  ```

[ASYNC][!WAIT] Handle async operations properly:
  ```javascript
  test("fetches and displays data", async () => {
    render(<Component />);
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText(/data loaded/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
    });
  });
  ```

[FORMS][!CONTROLLED] Test form interactions realistically:
  ```javascript
  const input = screen.getByLabelText(/email/i);
  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'test@example.com' } });
  expect(input.value).toBe('test@example.com');
  ```

[PERF][!FAST] Keep tests fast:
  - Mock heavy computations
  - Avoid unnecessary renders
  - Use shallow mocking where appropriate
  - Target < 1 second per test file

[QUALITY][!READABLE] Write clear, maintainable tests:
  - Use descriptive test names
  - Keep tests focused on single behaviors
  - Avoid test implementation details
  - Make assertions meaningful

[ACCESSIBILITY][!A11Y] Ensure components are accessible:
  - Test keyboard navigation
  - Verify ARIA labels
  - Check focus management
  - Validate semantic HTML

[BROWSER][!LIMITATION] Known Browser Automation Issue:
  - Playwright/browser automation tools may not trigger React synthetic events
  - For manual verification, create simple HTML test pages
  - Unit tests with mocked stores are the source of truth
  - Example: `/public/component_test.html` (remember to clean up after)

[CLEANUP][!ARTIFACTS] After manual browser testing:
  - Remove any `public/*_test.html` files
  - Delete temporary test components
  - Remove debug console.logs
  - Clean up unused mocks

Reference: docs/frontend_testing_guide.md
